<p>An endowment fund has been established with the ND Community Foundation. The fund will remain a permanent restricted endowment fund to assist the Mandan Historical Society to accomplish its mission. As with other endowment funds, the principal will remain invested in perpetuity. Only the earnings will be dispersed to support ongoing activities.</p>

<div class="fund-balance">
  <div>
    <h2>Build our fund !</h2>
    <p>Fund Balance</p>
    <strong>EOY 2024 $19,197.00</strong>
  </div>
  <img src="/assets/images/endowment/endowment-fund.jpg" alt="Coins and a growing plant">
</div>

<p>Its income can serve as a source of matching funds, vital to qualify for grants and a steady source of income for programming, projects, events or museum displays.</p>

<p>Dispursements have been made during 2021, 2022 and 2024 operational years to cover costs associated with the website and support development of museum displays.</p>

<p>Help us to build the principal! Donate today.</p>

<p>Family &amp; friends of these individuals funded an endowed memorial in their honor:</p>

<p class="memorial-name"><strong><em>Eldo Johnson</em></strong></p>

<p>Donations can be sent to the Mandan Historical Society, or directly to the ND Community Foundation at PO Box 387 Bismarck, ND 58502-0387 marked for Mandan Historical Society Endowment Fund. Information can be obtained by contacting Kara Geiger with ND Community Foundation in Bismarck at (701) 415-0984 or via email at <a href="mailto:kdvorak@ndcf.net">kara@ndcf.net</a>. A donation can also be made online via their <a href="http://www.ndcf.net/">www.ndcf.net</a> website.</p>
